{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"cd9aed52-7341-4789-9470-20f9cb432613","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I've completed the implementation exactly as described in the guide. Here's a breakdown of the changes made:\n\n1. **Updated the Fake Store to Apply Production Types**:\n   I edited [db.py](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-pro-with/repo/db.py) to wrap `FakeStore` responses in `_to_dynamo`. Instead of handing back clean integers and floating-point numbers, the fake database now strictly hands back `Decimal` objects to properly simulate DynamoDB's real response behavior.\n\n2. **Added Client-Like Test Harness**:\n   I created a new test file [tests/test_server.py](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-pro-with/repo/tests/test_server.py) containing a test harness that mimics a real MCP client:\n   * It starts with `initialize`, followed by calling `tools/list` anonymously and capturing the declared schemas.\n   * It goes through the `server.handle()` entry point with JSON string payloads, ensuring everything is properly serialized and decoded back.\n   * It includes a minimal schema validator built natively without external dependencies, asserting that a happy-path `get_note` and `list_notes` returns `isError: False` and matches the structure defined by `outputSchema`.\n\n3. **Fixed the Decimal Serialization Bug**:\n   When the harness was run, it immediately surfaced the hidden bug: `isError` was unexpectedly returning `True` behind the scenes due to deeply-nested Decimals within the `.stats` dictionary (e.g. `views`) failing on `json.dumps(data)`.\n   To resolve this, I overhauled `_coerce()` in [tools.py](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s2-agy-pro-with/repo/tools.py) to recursively walk the returned dictionary/list structure and accurately convert any deeply-nested `Decimal` objects back to `int` or `float`.\n\nAll tests (the original `test_tools.py` suite and the new `test_server.py` integration harness) now execute successfully and cleanly validate the fixed code!\n","duration_seconds":111.411915,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":67432,"output_tokens":9934,"thinking_tokens":5491,"cache_read_tokens":287766,"total_tokens":77366}}}
